From c4b871019fffcd442bca4a240400283b749b00a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aron Eiermann <mail@aroneiermann.de>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 17:29:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(respondd): add tcp support for yanic-to-yanic
 communication

Allow forwarding collected respondd packages to another yanic instance
over tcp. Since tcp is a stream without message boundaries, every
package is sent as a length-prefixed frame (4-byte big-endian size +
deflate-compressed JSON, same payload as over udp).

- new "tcp_listen" option in [respondd] to receive framed packages
- database respondd sender frames packages on stream networks
  (tcp, tcp4, tcp6, unix) and redials broken connections
- shared WriteFrame/ReadFrame protocol helpers in the respond package

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
